==== What is CWIST? =====
CWIST is a acronym of "C Web development Is Still Trustworthy".
This aims for modern, and fast C web framework.

A high-performance, C17 web framework that brings modern ergonomics
(HTTP/3, WebTransport, Post-Quantum TLS, zero-copy I/O) to systems
programming without sacrificing control.
Powered by BoringSSL, lsquic, OpenSSL without context contamination.

Two server modes, tuned for opposite things; pick per workload.
CWIST reactor is the default (no env var needed); CWIST_C1M_MODE=0 selects
CWIST Classic pool.

  CWIST reactor (default)  takes the throughput. Many connections per event
                           loop, so a connection costs a reactor slot, not a
                           parked thread. On the run below: 142,258 req/s
                           against Axum's 114,649, 24% more.

  CWIST Classic pool       takes the latency. A thread per connection, so no
                           request waits behind another in a batch. Median
                           1.55ms against Axum's 3.21ms, and ahead through
                           p99.

The distribution, not the average, is the point:

                    p50      p90      p99    p99.9  p99.999
  CWIST Classic   1.55ms   4.12ms   7.35ms  13.30ms  29.39ms
  CWIST           1.99ms   7.86ms  15.06ms  19.58ms  25.82ms
  Axum            3.21ms   5.78ms   8.61ms  11.57ms  18.09ms

Classic pool leads for the first 99% of requests and both modes answer
the median faster. The crossover is at p99.9, where Axum's extreme tail
is tighter; closing that is open work.


==================================================================
 WHY CWIST?
==================================================================

* "Why not just use Axum (Rust) or Gin (Go)?" -- CWIST's True Niche
  At first glance, one might ask: Why use a C-based web framework
  when modern memory-safe languages with massive ecosystems exist?

== PAST ROADMAP ==

- Security: CORS middleware and origin / header policy management.
- RestAPI: Dedicated features for optimized RestAPI server deployment.
